      "math_academy_id": "q-43892",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Given that $\\{i,j\\}$ is the standard basis of ${R}^{2}$ and that the images of $i$ and $j$ under the action of a linear transformation $T$ are $⟨1,4⟩$ and $⟨5,-1⟩$, respectively, what is the standard matrix of $T?$",
      "worked_solution": "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{2}$ can be represented as a $2\\times 2$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i$ and $j$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for this linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
